FYDE: mfd: rp1: restore PCI state after firmware reset on resume

rp1_resume() (added in 041-fix-kernel-warning-in-suspending) re-triggers
the RP1 firmware by calling reset_control_reset() and then restores only
RP1's private MSI-X cfg registers. But that reset runs in the regular
resume phase, AFTER the PCI core has already restored RP1's config space
and MSI-X table in the noirq phase. The reset returns the RP1 PCIe
endpoint to its power-on state, wiping the BARs, bus-master-enable and
the MSI-X table -- and nothing reprograms them.

The result: after system resume RP1 register/MMIO access still works (so
the PCIe link and the macb PHY report "up"), but no downstream peripheral
can DMA to system memory or raise MSI-X interrupts. The ethernet link
comes up at 1Gbps yet moves zero packets (TX=0, RX all errors), DHCP
fails, and even unbind/rebind of the macb driver cannot recover it. A
full PCI remove+rescan of RP1 (which reprograms everything after the
reset) does recover it -- confirming the missing step is the post-reset
PCI reprogramming, not anything in the child drivers.

Fix: snapshot the good PCI state at the start of rp1_resume (it was
restored by the core in the noirq phase), then after the firmware reset
call pci_restore_state() to reprogram the config space and MSI-X table,
mirroring probe's order (reset first, then configure).

BUG=none
TEST=powerd_dbus_suspend on rpi5; eth0 gets a DHCP lease and passes traffic after resume
Index: v6.12-rpi/drivers/mfd/rp1.c
===================================================================
--- v6.12-rpi.orig/drivers/mfd/rp1.c
+++ v6.12-rpi/drivers/mfd/rp1.c
@@ -374,9 +374,22 @@ static int rp1_suspend(struct device *de
 static int rp1_resume(struct device *dev)
 {
 	struct rp1_dev *rp1 = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
+	struct pci_dev *pdev = rp1->pdev;
 	u32 chip_id;
 	int i, retries;
 
+	/*
+	 * Snapshot the good PCI state that the PCI core restored during the
+	 * noirq resume phase. The firmware reset below returns the RP1 PCIe
+	 * endpoint to its power-on state, clearing the BARs, bus-master enable
+	 * and the MSI-X table; we reprogram them afterwards with
+	 * pci_restore_state() so the downstream peripherals (ethernet, USB)
+	 * can DMA and raise interrupts again. Without this the datapath
+	 * silently dies on resume even though the link and register access
+	 * still work (link reports up, but TX/RX move no packets).
+	 */
+	pci_save_state(pdev);
+
 	/* Re-trigger RP1 firmware initialisation after PCIe power cycle */
 	reset_control_reset(rp1->reset);
 
@@ -396,6 +409,13 @@ static int rp1_resume(struct device *dev
 			 "RP1 firmware not ready after resume (chip_id=0x%x)\n",
 			 chip_id);
 
+	/*
+	 * Reprogram the config space (BARs, command/bus-master) and MSI-X
+	 * table that the firmware reset cleared, mirroring the order used at
+	 * probe time (reset first, then configure).
+	 */
+	pci_restore_state(pdev);
+
 	for (i = 0; i < RP1_IRQS; i++)
 		writel(rp1->msix_cfg_saved[i], rp1->msix_cfg_regs + MSIX_CFG(i));
 
